Context:
- Added project environment setup for Clojure development with Emacs
- Integrated tmux session management for isolated development environments
- Configuration supports CIDER, paredit, and org-mode for literate programming

Considerations:
- Used PROJECT_NAME and PROJECT_ROOT as overridable variables
- Made Emacs configuration dynamically generated to avoid hardcoded paths
- Chose tmux for session management to provide TTY access
- Included package auto-installation for seamless setup

Issues addressed:
- Need for isolated development environments per project
- Support for Clojure tooling (CIDER, paredit)
- Integration with existing shadow-cljs build system
- Compatibility with literate programming approach (.org files)

Timing:
- Implementation date: 2025-08-06
- Development time: ~10 minutes
- Testing confirmed: Emacs config generation, tmux session commands

Technical details:
- Emacs launched with -Q flag for clean environment
- Configuration loaded via -l flag for project isolation
- TTY accessible via tmux list-panes for external tool integration
